  "description": "DESIGN\nThe design proposes to construct a 6m Rear extension. \nThe Rear extension is designed with part flat roof and part sloped roof incorporating two roof lights, one window and a door facing the rear garden. \n\nSCALE\nThe depth of the rear extension would be no more than 6m. The eaves height would be 2.90m and 3.94m at the highest point. The open Space around the original house would be approx. 78% after the rear extension which is above 50% benchmark. \n\nMATERIAL\nThe finish material of the rear extension would be External render matching with the existing rear facade. The windows and doors all would be of White uPVC. The flat roof of the extension will be finished with fiber glass with top coat or similar.\n\nACCESS\nThe existing front access will be used to enter the house.\n\nPLANNING HISTORY\n1256/25 Prior Approval - Householders: Single storey rear extension with a depth of 6.00 metres, highest point of 3.50 metres and height at the eaves of 3.00 metres. 12 Jun 2025 - Refused.\n\nSUMMARY\nThe design proposal creates harmonious relationship between the existing and proposed forms with its modest scale and proportion, adopting traditional design and using existing matching materials. It also complies with Schedule-2 Part-1 Class-A of the Town and Country Planning Order 1995. Thus humbly request to grant prior approval for the proposed design.",
  "application_type_full": "Prior Approval: Larger Home Extension"
}